      "remaining_part": "The native Windows runtime reader threads append fh.read() only at EOF. Its _communicate timeout raises TimeoutExpired(args,timeout) without output/stderr. If a second communicate also times out (for example, a surviving descendant retains an inherited pipe), both captured snapshots remain empty even when the client has emitted bytes; no raw stream file or incremental buffer exists. The passing simple-timeout fixture already records an empty first_timeout_streams and recovers output only because its second communicate reaches EOF. Strict UTF-8 text decoding can also discard undecodable output in the reader thread instead of preserving raw bytes.",
